  "boundaries": [
    "Six independent replay histories are actual stable 3/4/5-voter EMPTY/backup bootstraps and first BARRIER applications, not automatic network dispatch or public runtime.",
    "Two fresh JVMs reopen the same original storage, re-force its certificate/end and expose identical target metadata. They do not add crash or power-loss qualification.",
    "Separate Java lifecycle checks use a real typed DATA target and real checkpoint quorum publication; those histories are retained but not included in the independent six-history BARRIER replay.",
    "Both isolated builds use identical production Java bytes. The supplemental lifecycle class was added after the first build; 15 plus two tests are distinct executions, not a claim of a full reactor suite.",
    "The first independent replay drafts had verifier-only variable-shadowing and directory-inventory errors. Corrections replay unchanged original Java files. See oracle-diagnostics.json.",
    "No ledger update, future-proof persistence, raw-byte authority constructor, new disk/wire format, image-slot increase or selector publication is introduced by the capability.",
    "Durable future retention, original-source and selected transfer, actual quorum-gated dispatch, automatic offline-survivor continuation and all remaining Phase 3 gates stay open."
  ],
